   - An event listener is added to the file input element (`id="imageUpload"`).
   - When a file is selected, the script checks the MIME type of the selected file.
   - It then compares the MIME type against the list of allowed image types.
   - If the MIME type does not match any of the allowed types, an alert box will appear indicating that only image files are allowed.

This approach ensures that the user cannot select other file types than those specified in the `accept` attribute, thus restricting the file upload to images only.

