<pre><code>var validation_messages = {
    &quot;key_1&quot;: {
        &quot;your_name&quot;: &quot;jimmy&quot;,
        &quot;your_msg&quot;: &quot;hello world&quot;
    },
    &quot;key_2&quot;: {
        &quot;your_name&quot;: &quot;billy&quot;,
        &quot;your_msg&quot;: &quot;foo equals bar&quot;
    }
}
</code></pre>

answer:
To loop through all members in a JavaScript object, including values that are objects, you can use a `for...in` loop or `Object.keys()` method combined with a `forEach()` function.

Here's an example of how you can use both methods:

### Using `for...in` Loop

```javascript
var validation_messages = {
    "key_1": {
        "your_name": "jimmy",
        "your_msg": "hello world"
    },
    "key_2": {
        "your_name": "billy",
        "your_msg": "foo equals bar"
    }
};

// Using for...in loop
for (var key in validation_messages) {
    if (validation_messages.hasOwnProperty(key)) {
        var obj = validation_messages[key];
        console.log('Key:', key);
        console.log('Your Name:', obj.your_name);
        console.log('Your Message:', obj.your_msg);
        console.log('-');
    }
}
```

### Using `Object.keys()` Method Combined with `forEach()`

```javascript
var validation_messages = {
    "key_1": {
        "your_name": "jimmy",
        "your_msg": "hello world"
    },
    "key_2": {
        "your_name": "billy",
        "your_msg": "foo equals bar"
    }
};

// Using Object.keys() and forEach()
Object.keys(validation_messages).forEach(function(key) {
    var obj = validation_messages[key];
    console.log('Key:', key);
    console.log('Your Name:', obj.your_name);
    console.log('Your Message:', obj.your_msg);
    console.log('-');
});
```

Both methods will output:
```
Key: key_1
Your Name: jimmy
Your Message: hello world
-

Key: key_2
Your Name: billy
Your Message: foo equals bar
-
```

This approach ensures that all properties of the object, regardless of whether they are strings, numbers, arrays, functions, or other objects themselves, are accessed and processed.

